{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_metrics", "label": "Stock metrics", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_actor_lifecycle_metrics", "label": "Actor lifecycle and message metrics", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Created, terminated, restarted and messages-delivered counters, each a single unlabeled series recorded across the whole system."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_actor_message_handler_seconds", "label": "actor_message_handler_seconds", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Time spent inside onReceive handlers on the default seconds-scale buckets; its p99 is the how-slow-is-a-handler signal."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_actor_mailbox_size", "label": "actor_mailbox_size", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The backlog signal. Mailboxes are unbounded by default, so an actor that falls behind accumulates rather than sheds, and a series exists only once one crosses 10 000 queued messages - its presence is therefore the alert, and on a healthy system the metric is empty. The path label is constitutive rather than descriptive: a depth gauge without it would have every actor of a class overwriting its siblings within one sampling pass."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_actor_mailbox_wait_seconds", "label": "actor_mailbox_wait_seconds", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The latency signal, and the half the handler histogram cannot give you - that one starts measuring once a message is already being handled, so a slow actor and a merely-behind actor look identical in it. Its buckets run 1 ms to 10 s rather than the default ladder, because a mailbox that is keeping up drains well under the 5 ms the defaults start at and a histogram whose first bucket holds everything answers nothing. Replayed stashed messages and messages queued before metrics were on are deliberately excluded; throttled messages are counted."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_actor_mailbox_dropped_total", "label": "actor_mailbox_dropped_total", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The shedding signal, appearing only for actors somebody deliberately bounded. It counts per class, not per actor: a bounded mailbox sheds as its designed steady state rather than as an anomaly, so a path-labelled counter minted a permanent series for every actor working as intended - and under sharding the value came from whoever addressed the shard region. Pass your own onDrop if you need per-instance detail; it fires alongside the stock counter rather than replacing it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_actor_dead_letters_total", "label": "actor_dead_letters_total", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A loss signal, not a backlog one: any sustained non-zero rate means messages are being sent to actors that are not there. Only present once the dead-letter store is something other than off, since the counter is minted by the queue. The recipient label is what makes one letter distinguishable from another and is bounded in practice by the registry per-family cap."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_cluster_metrics", "label": "Cluster metrics", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Members up, gossip rounds, gossip records refused and envelope-from mismatches. The refusal reasons are a closed set of four, and the envelope-mismatch frame label is drawn from code and never from the payload - the claimed address is deliberately not a label, because that would mint one series per address a sender cares to invent."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_distributed_data_metrics", "label": "DistributedData metrics", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The CRDT replicator quorum path and its wire decoder - four families contributing six series in total. Rejected and timed-out separate the two failure shapes: refused means the request never started, timed out means it started and nobody answered in time. Dropped values is not a tuning signal at all - a peer is sending payloads this replica cannot decode."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_projection_metrics", "label": "Projection metrics", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A projection is a background loop nobody watches, which is exactly the kind of thing that fails quietly. Stalled is published as 0 when a projection starts so the series exists for every running projection and equals-1 is a working alert expression; separating handler from poll failures separates the two fixes, and events-skipped is the data-loss signal."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_label_rule", "label": "The stock-label rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A stock label values must be bounded by what the deployment declares - never by traffic volume, by how many actors have been spawned, or by a value a remote party supplies. Two labels stay per-instance for stated reasons; the mailbox-drop counter used to carry a path label and no longer does, because it satisfied neither test."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_metrics_overhead", "label": "Stock metrics overhead", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "There is no opt-out flag - stock metrics are always wired in. Until enable, every instrumentation call resolves against a noop registry, a single object lookup that records nothing."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_metrics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_actor_lifecycle_metrics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_metrics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_actor_message_handler_seconds", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_metrics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_actor_mailbox_size", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_metrics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_actor_mailbox_wait_seconds", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_metrics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_actor_mailbox_dropped_total", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_metrics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_actor_dead_letters_total", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_metrics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_cluster_metrics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_metrics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_distributed_data_metrics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_metrics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_projection_metrics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_metrics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_label_rule", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_metrics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_stock_metrics_overhead", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/stock-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_obs